            "text": "Before the invention of Johannes Gutenberg’s movable-type printing press around 1440, books were painstakingly copied by hand. Because they were extremely rare and expensive, children rarely used books in school. Instead, lessons relied heavily on oral memorization, recitation, and teachers reading aloud from a single manuscript.\n\nThe printing press revolutionized"
